      "message": "This is a major dependency upgrade on a stable branch -- outside the normal \"bug fixes only\" policy. I\u0027d like to flag the reasoning so the exception is deliberate.\n\n3.14.0 has shipped, so this rolls out starting with 3.14.1 - unusual for a point release. But the alternative (Jetty 9 across the remaining 3.14.x lifecycle) is worse: Jetty 9 is EOL, the 9.4.x patches available now are customer-sponsored extended-support only, and Maven Central stops publishing them in early 2026. After that cutoff we cannot bump Jetty 9 even if a CVE requires it.\n\nWhat makes the risk acceptable: no source-level API break for plugins (javax.servlet + Guice preserved; the ee8 adapter is the Jetty project\u0027s documented Servlet-4 interim path), and the diff is scope-bounded - see commit message.\n\nI wouldn\u0027t normally backport a change of this size. The EOL clock on Jetty 9 is what shifts the trade-off.",
